# conf/agent-bundle.manifest — the fleet's Agent configuration as ONE package
# (issue #1725, EPIC #1718 C7): what a full install (~/.claude/fleet, a git
# checkout) and a client-only computer (~/.local/share/claude-fleet, from the
# hub's /install or GitHub's stable) both get, from the same files.
#
#   <repo-relative path>  <category>
#
# A path ending in `/` is every file under it, recursively, except a name that
# starts with `.` or `_` (list such a file on its own line). `#` starts a
# comment. Categories are what `fleet doctor`'s agents line counts — hooks ·
# skills · mcp · mod (the four the EPIC's metric reads), plus settings /
# commands (filled with them) and tool (what applies the rest).
#
# Read in three places, maintained here only:
#   · bin/fleet-agent-bundle.py   files / version / check — the expansion
#   · bin/fleet-client-mirror.sh  writes the expansion into the hub's client
#                                 manifest (its generated `agent bundle` block);
#                                 bin/fleet-client-pack.sh packs the files into
#                                 a hub build (#1803)
#   · bin/fleet-install-apply.sh  --bundle: the apply a client runs (fill only;
#                                 the override files always win)
# Version = a digest of these files' bytes (`fleet-agent-bundle.py version`),
# so a checkout at stable and a client installed from it print the same one.

# hooks — the table, the guards it wires, and the shim a client wires them through
hooks/settings-hooks.json           hooks
hooks/agent-guard.py                hooks
hooks/artifact-guard.py             hooks
hooks/base-readonly-guard.py        hooks
hooks/bash-guard.py                 hooks
bin/fleet-hook-run.sh               hooks
bin/fleet-hook-personal.sh          hooks

# settings — the default Claude Code keys (#1558)
conf/claude-settings.default.json   settings

# MCP + the doc block + Codex's posture (#1559), and the two servers' wrappers
conf/agent-defaults/                mcp
bin/mcp-github.sh                   mcp
bin/mcp-fetch.sh                    mcp

# skills — Claude's ~/.claude/skills and Codex's $CODEX_HOME/skills
skills/                             skills

# commands — Claude's slash commands, and Codex's native-skill copies of them
commands/                           commands
conf/codex-preamble.md              commands

# mod — the in-session plugin (#1335) every fleet-launched Claude loads
mod/fleet/.claude-plugin/plugin.json  mod
mod/fleet/hooks/                    mod
mod/fleet/types/                    mod
mod/fleet/tsconfig.json             mod

# tool — what applies the package
bin/fleet-agent-bundle.py           tool
bin/fleet-install-apply.sh          tool
bin/fleet-hooks-merge.py            tool
bin/fleet-agent-defaults.py         tool
bin/fleet-agent-team.py             tool
bin/fleet-config.py                 tool
# the roles' definitions + the rule table, and their one reader / writer: the
# fleet-config skill (#2785) runs `fleet role …` on a client-only computer too
bin/fleet-role.py                   tool
bin/fleet_rules.py                  tool
agents/                             tool
conf/role-rules.default.md          tool
bin/fleet-daemon-lib.sh             tool

# the credential proxy every session reaches its subscription through (#1970):
# a client-only computer runs it too (`fleet-cred-proxy.sh ensure`)
bin/fleet-cred-proxy.sh             tool
bin/fleet-cred-proxy.py             tool
# its pass for the Singapore relay, minted when the relay road is configured (#1974)
bin/fleet-relay-cred.sh             tool
# a session on a client-only computer, through that proxy (#2136): `fleet run
# claude|codex` mints the hub pass with fleet-session-cred.sh; `fleet cred-scan`
# counts what a session there can reach
bin/fleet-run.sh                    tool
bin/fleet-session-cred.sh           tool
bin/fleet-cred-scan.py              tool
